(1 Master + 1 Worker)
This is a production-style Kubernetes setup.
## Architecture

     +---------------------+
 |      Control Plane Node      |
 |      (Master Node)           |
      +---------------------+
                 |
                 |  
      +---------------------+
   |       Worker Node        |
      +---------------------+

##Prerequisites
Create 2 EC2 instances:
Node     Master              Worker  
Type    c7i.flex.large     t3.medium

Security Group
Allow:
Port        Protocol     Purpose
22           TCP           SSH
6443         TCP       Kubernetes API
2379-2380    TCP          etcd
10250        TCP         Kubelet
10257        TCP       Controller Manager
10259        TCP        Scheduler
30000-32767  TCP      NodePort Services
For learning, you can temporarily allow all traffic between the two instances' security groups.

Step 1: Run on BOTH Master and Worker Nodes
Update System
sudo dnf update -y

Disable Swap
Check swap:
free -h

Disable: sudo swapoff -a

Make permanent:
sudo sed -i '/swap/d' /etc/fstab

Verify:
swapon --show   ------ No output should appear.

Configure Kernel Modules

cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/k8s.conf
overlay
br_netfilter
EOF

Load modules:
sudo modprobe overlay
sudo modprobe br_netfilter

Configure Networking
cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/k8s.conf
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables = 1
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables = 1
net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1
EOF

Apply:
sudo sysctl --system
Verify:
sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward

Expected:
net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1


Step 2: Install Container Runtime (containerd)
Run on BOTH nodes.
Install:
sudo dnf install containerd -y

Create configuration:
sudo mkdir -p /etc/containerd
containerd config default | sudo tee /etc/containerd/config.toml

Enable Systemd Cgroup

Edit:
sudo vi /etc/containerd/config.toml

Find:
SystemdCgroup = false

Change to:
SystemdCgroup = true

Save and exit.

Start service:
sudo systemctl enable containerd
sudo systemctl restart containerd

Check:
sudo systemctl status containerd

Step 3: Install Kubernetes Packages
Run on BOTH nodes.

Add Kubernetes repository:
cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/yum.repos.d/kubernetes.repo
[kubernetes]
name=Kubernetes
baseurl=https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.33/rpm/
enabled=1
gpgcheck=1
gpgkey=https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.33/rpm/repodata/repomd.xml.key
EOF


Install packages:
sudo dnf install -y kubelet kubeadm kubectl

Enable kubelet:
sudo systemctl enable kubelet

Verify:
kubeadm version
kubectl version --client

Step 4: Initialize Master Node
Run ONLY on MASTER.
Find private IP:
hostname -I

Example:  172.31.10.100

Initialize cluster:

sudo kubeadm init \
--pod-network-cidr=192.168.0.0/16
Wait 2–5 minutes.

Configure kubectl for ec2-user

After successful initialization:

mkdir -p $HOME/.kube
sudo cp -i /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf $HOME/.kube/config
sudo chown $(id -u):$(id -g) $HOME/.kube/config

Verify:

kubectl get nodes
Output:
  NAME          STATUS 
  k8s-master    NotReady
This is expected until a network plugin is installed.

Step 5: Install Calico Network Plugin
Run on MASTER.
Apply Calico:
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/projectcalico/calico/v3.30.0/manifests/calico.yaml

Check pods:

kubectl get pods -A
Wait until all pods are Running.

Check node:
kubectl get nodes

Expected:

NAME          STATUS
k8s-master    Ready

Step 6: Join Worker Node
On MASTER, get join command:

kubeadm token create --print-join-command
Example output:

kubeadm join 172.31.10.100:6443 --token abcdef.1234567890abcdef --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:xxxxxxxx
Copy the entire command.

Run Join Command on WORKER
SSH into worker node.

Run:

sudo kubeadm join 172.31.10.100:6443 --token abcdef.1234567890abcdef --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:xxxxxxxx

Expected:

This node has joined the cluster

Step 7: Verify Worker Joined

On MASTER:

kubectl get nodes
Expected:

NAME           STATUS
k8s-master     Ready
k8s-worker1    Ready
kubectl label node ip-172-31-15-86.ap-south-1.compute.internal  noderole.kubernetes.io/worker=worker

Step 8: Deploy First Application
Create deployment:
kubectl create deployment nginx --image=bhagyash654/batch:v2

Scale deployment:
kubectl scale deployment nginx --replicas=3

Check pods:
kubectl get pods -o wide

Example:

NAME                    NODE
nginx-xxx               k8s-worker1
nginx-yyy               k8s-master
nginx-zzz               k8s-worker1
Pods will be distributed across nodes.

Step 9: Expose Application

kubectl expose deployment nginx --port=80 --target-port=80 --type=NodePort

Check:
kubectl get svc

Example:
nginx   NodePort   80:31245/TCP

Access:
http://<Worker-Public-IP>:31245

or

http://<Master-Public-IP>:31245

Important Troubleshooting Commands

Check Nodes : kubectl get nodes
Check Pods  : kubectl get pods -A
Describe Node  : kubectl describe node k8s-worker1
View Logs : kubectl logs <pod-name>
Check Kubelet : sudo systemctl status kubelet
Check Containerd : sudo systemctl status containerd
